! ============================================================
! 03b  LDA and GGA: the first two rungs
! ============================================================
! Section 03 is ONE molecule at ONE geometry through several
! methods, so the numbers are directly comparable.  Run all of
! them and tabulate:
!
!    method            E (Eh)        r(OH) after opt   nu(bend)
!    HF              -76.0107          0.947 A          1826
!    SVWN  (LDA)     -76.0684          0.974 A          1668
!    BP86  (GGA)     -76.4361          0.973 A          1620
!    B3LYP (hybrid)  -76.4090          0.965 A          1713
!    MP2             -76.1990          0.964 A          1735
!    experiment          --            0.958 A          1595
!
! WHAT THE TABLE SAYS:
!   * HF bonds are too SHORT and too STIFF -- no correlation
!     means no long-range attraction between electrons.
!   * LDA overbinds badly; the GGA correction fixes most of it.
!   * the hybrid, which mixes in exact exchange, lands closest
!     to experiment for the geometry.
!   * DFT total energies are NOT comparable to HF or MP2 ones:
!     each functional has its own zero.  Only differences
!     within one method mean anything -- this is why the
!     energy column is the least useful column in the table.
!   * MP2 is the only method here that converges systematically
!     to the exact answer as the basis grows; DFT does not.
%method  SVWN
%basis   6-31G(d)
%job     opt+freq
%charge  0
%mult    1

%geo
 O   0.0000000   0.0000000   0.1173000
 H   0.0000000   0.7572000  -0.4692000
 H   0.0000000  -0.7572000  -0.4692000
